  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increase the resilience of conflict affected population through improved access to life-saving WASH services and supplies in eastern and southern oblasts of Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PIN proposes a package of activities to address WASH-related humanitarian needs. This includes:1.Rehabilitation of damaged water supply systems, responding to the shortage in accessing water resulted by the attacks on the water and energy infrastructure particularly in the frontline areas.2.Establishment of social laundry centres, to restore the access to laundry service especially in areas closer to the frontline and/or de-occupied areas where the access to water and energy is not stable/ available on the household level, and people returned to their house but cannot access such service, and considering remarkable percentage of elderly and PWD  who need access to laundry more often due to their especial hygiene needs.3.Provision of hygiene items through in-kind or through a cash modality that aims to enhance the access to hygiene materials for most vulnerable of crises-affected population in frontline areas.</narrative>
  </description>
